{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779750948,"nonce":"fqfGbYftkoFVEAv27fSq0qTRTu8=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDnsOvg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/167#issuecomment-4537913022"},"message":"**Tie-off — analysis complete; durable deliverable landed in [PR #176](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/176) (merged).**\n\nThe cross-deployment power characterization across the single 2026-05-19 → 21 → 22 charge cycle is done. The durable reference is **[`bizzyboat_project11/docs/bizzyboat_power.md`](../blob/jazzy/bizzyboat_project11/docs/bizzyboat_power.md)** (battery system, measured current anchors, discharge characterization, the sensor-free power model + limits, and the operational deployment-planning rules). The detailed working analysis lives at `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05_charge_cycle_findings.md` (the issue's \"goes in `~/data`\" deliverable).\n\n### Scope → outcome\n| # | Sub-analysis | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| ① | Cross-deployment battery model | Plateau→knee discharge curve across the 3-deployment cycle; bounded energy; ~273 Ah pack (derived). **Recharge curve = open gap** — the post-recovery bag was too short; measure a full charge next opportunity (for cohort-swap planning). |\n| ② | Sag-vs-SOC | **Corrected**: load sag is *small* (~0.05–0.12 V) and only *mildly* SOC-dependent, reproducible across **7 deployments / ~3 months**. The earlier \"~10× with SOC\" was a within-deployment SOC-drift artifact, removed by SOC-matched pairing. R_int ≈ stable; the strong dependence is on **PWM**, not SOC. |\n| ③ | Speed-power (1/2/4 kt anchors) | At fixed throttle the drop is largest near static (bollard) and shrinks ~0.3–0.4 V as the boat speeds up (prop unloads). The 67 A full-throttle anchor is the *running* load; bollard/accel current is higher. |\n| ④ | Phase-by-phase draw | **Idle/hotel load dominates the budget** — the pack drains even dockside. Charge to full before each deployment day; power gabby down between groups. |\n\n### Precision caveat\nAll current / power / energy / endurance figures are **modeled (±~30 %)** — there is no current sensor on this hull (`BATT_MONITOR 3`, `BATT_CURR_PIN -1`; voltage is the only real electrical measurement). Tightening these to real numbers is gated on the **PWM × current sweep → #88** (the unlock). What *is* measured and reliable — and what operators/students should actually use — is the **voltage ladder** (pre-launch resting-V go/no-go + in-mission loaded-V recovery ladder) in the doc.\n\n### Follow-ups carried elsewhere\n- **#88** — PWM × current sweep + dockside idle clamp + optional measured capacity (removes the ±30 %).\n- **#171 / #162** — annunciator never warns at LVD → manual voltage watch required today (class-blocking).\n- Recharge curve — uncharacterized; measure a full charge for cohort-swap planning.\n\nClosing as **complete**; the remaining precision work is #88's.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1779750949,"nonce":"+kD71rvtSr1tt+NS5dV46NxGuf8=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ7JHc8AAAAGCk9ZOw"},"status":2}]}